## CPU Instruction Flow

The CPU follows the general process:

    1. PC contains instruction address
             ↓
    2. Instruction fetched
             ↓
    3. Instruction decoded
             ↓
    4. Registers read
             ↓
    5. ALU operation performed
             ↓
    6. Memory accessed if required
             ↓
    7. Result written to register
             ↓
    8. PC updated

This repeats for every instruction.

---

## Machine Code

RISC-V assembly instructions are eventually converted into machine code.

For example:

    ADD x5, x6, x7

is encoded as a 32-bit instruction.

The CPU does not directly understand the text:

    ADD x5, x6, x7

Instead, it receives the binary instruction.

The process is:

    RISC-V Assembly
          ↓
       Assembler
          ↓
    Machine Code
          ↓
    Instruction Memory
          ↓
       RISC-V CPU

This is how real software eventually reaches the hardware.

